  "implementation": [
    "NativeSignalRead exposes current signal metadata/readers without any conversion to NativeMediaRead. Named source dtmf.send and recipient dtmf.receive do not require connection.offer or stream.subscribe.",
    "Canonical authentication derives the protocol data floor for dtmf.send/dtmf.receive independently of messaging and Session/media/subscription floors. The owned audio SDK preserves an explicit server permission refusal as an Application error.",
    "Current credential epochs, separately enrolled Device/key, exact physical source/generation, current original Session audience, private/handoff pair restrictions, both recipient ceilings and actual registration remain mandatory. Frozen recipients govern DTMF replay/result authority; original offer resources remain a locking footprint.",
    "Physical lifetime polling now checks current ownership/binding and original Session access without treating missing RTP permission as source retirement. It returns only a transient boolean observation and no IO grant; current credential revocation still invalidates it. Moved replacement lifetime polling resolves the installed current origin.",
    "Credential metadata rotation uses current Binding/physical ownership rather than requiring the predecessor to retain media permission. Non-DTMF native stream step-up retains its earlier explicit media-scope refusal.",
    "Production real human consent requests only dtmf.send, rotates the same physical source and resumes the unchanged held envelope/logical operation. Independent cases prove fresh signaling after receive-only refresh, and refused newly sent RTP with a fully authorized receiver after an actual PCMU baseline.",
    "Production receiver refresh uses only dtmf.receive and a separately enrolled current credential on the original Device/key, then receives a new actual signed signal. Audio subscription control under the send-only credential refuses before an operation is created. Both EdDSA and ES256 execute these cases."
  ],
